# Monad testnet, mock flow: our own mintable USDC and xStocks, hedges on MockDex, prices live from Kuru's books.
# Use this while you don't have Kuru's test tokens; it only needs MON for gas (roughly 5-15 MON for deploy + demo).
# The real flow (Kuru's tokens, hedging on Kuru) is contracts/monad-testnet.env.example.
#
# Copy to contracts/.env and fill in PRIVATE_KEY (never commit .env). Then, from the repo root:
#
#   npm run deploy:monad-testnet
#   cd backend && NETWORK=monadTestnet node src/index.js        (backend/.env: see the bottom of this file)
#
# What you get: every series, vault, lender and gap round deployed on Monad testnet, spots and strikes centred on
# Kuru's live NVDAx/TSLAx/SPYx mid prices, lenders and MockDex funded by the deploy, makers funded on start
# (mock tokens are mintable), and the reporter pushing Kuru's mid prices so option prices track the real books.
# Check the Kuru side any time (read-only): node backend/scripts/kuru-prices.mjs

PRIVATE_KEY=
MONAD_TESTNET_RPC=https://testnet-rpc.monad.xyz

# No USE_REAL_TOKENS: the deploy creates mock USDC/NVDAx/TSLAx/SPYx and a MockDex hedge venue.
# No KURU_ACCOUNT_CORE: no KuruAdapter, HedgedMaker hedges on MockDex at the oracle price.
# Kuru markets are recorded only as the price source:
KURU_MARKETS=NVDAx=0xE9C2B9E0F296dbeC9dcc3C8F0F64928F2F8bC081,TSLAx=0x7A53BB8d8A8765418FfE331A02BF5984264922AA,SPYx=0x185Af307dAfd968033337A0180E66B920B4b05Ca

# Optional: first expiry this many minutes from now (default: next Monday 9:30 ET open)
# EXPIRY_MINUTES=60

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# backend/.env for the same deployment (never commit). One funded key can play every role in a demo:
#   NETWORK=monadTestnet
#   REPORTER_KEY=0x...     PRICE_SOURCE=kuru is the default because the deployment records Kuru markets
#   KEEPER_KEY=0x...
#   OPERATOR_KEY=0x...     runs the HedgedMaker's quotes and hedge ratios
#   MAKER_KEYS=0x...       plain maker bots; on a mock deployment they mint their own inventory on start
#   HEDGE_MODE=off
#   ASK_SIZE=1             default on Monad testnet
#   BID_SIZE=1
